 674:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  Sets a new value for the specified parameter in the \ref group_structures.
 675:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *
 676:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** * \details
 677:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  This function sets the value of the specified parameter by the paramId 
 678:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  argument. The paramId for each register is available in the 
 679:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  CapSense RegisterMap header file as 
 680:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  CapSense_<ParameterName>_PARAM_ID. The paramId is a special 
 681:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  enumerated value generated by the customizer. The format of paramId is as 
 682:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  follows:
 683:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *    1. [ byte 3 byte 2 byte 1 byte 0 ] 
 684:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *    2. [ TTWFCCCC UIIIIIII MMMMMMMM LLLLLLLL ]
 685:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *    3. T - encodes the parameter type:
 686:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *      - 01b: uint8
 687:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *      - 10b: uint16
 688:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *      - 11b: uint32
 689:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *    4. W - indicates whether the parameter is writable:
 690:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *      - 0: ReadOnly
 691:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *      - 1: Read/Write
 692:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *    5. C - 4 bit CRC (X^3 + 1) of the whole paramId word, the C bits are 
 693:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *       filled with 0s when the CRC is calculated.
 694:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *    6. U - indicates if the parameter affects the RAM Widget Object CRC.
 695:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *    7. I - specifies that the widgetID parameter belongs to
 696:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *    8. M,L - the parameter offset MSB and LSB accordingly in:
 697:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *      - Flash Data Structure if W bit is 0.
 698:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *      - RAM Data Structure if W bit is 1.
 699:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *
 700:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  Refer to the \ref group_structures section for details of the data structure 
 701:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  organization and examples of its register access.
 702:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *
 703:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** * \param paramId  
 704:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  Specify the ID of parameter to set its value.
 705:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  A macro for the parameter ID can be found in the CapSense RegisterMap header
 706:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  file defined as CapSense_<ParameterName>_PARAM_ID.
