 928:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *
 929:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** * \brief
 930:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  Reports the status of the specified matrix button widget.
 931:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *
 932:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** * \details 
 933:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  This function reports if the specified matrix widget has detected a touch or
 934:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  not by extracting the information from the wdgtStatus registers 
 935:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  (CapSense_WDGT_STATUS<X>_VALUE for the CSD widgets and 
 936:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  CapSense_SNS_STATUS<WidgetId>_VALUE for CSX widget). In addition, the
 937:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  function provides details of the active sensor including active rows/columns 
 938:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  for the CSD widgets. This function should be used only with the matrix button
 939:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  widgets. This function does not process the widget, but extracts the 
 940:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  processed results from the \ref group_structures.
 941:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *
 942:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** * \param widgetId 
 943:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  Specify the ID number of the matrix button widget to check status of its 
 944:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  sensors. 
 945:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  A macro for widget ID can be found in the CapSense Configuration header file 
 946:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  defined as CapSense_<WidgetName>_WDGT_ID
 947:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *
 948:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** * \return 
 949:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  Returns the touch detection status of sensors in the specified matrix 
 950:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  buttons widget. Zero indicates that no touch is detected in the specified 
 951:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *  widget or a wrong widgetId is specified.
 952:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *    1. For the matrix buttons widgets with the CSD sensing mode:
 953:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *      - Bit [31] if set, indicates that one or more sensors in the widget 
 954:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *        detected a touch.
 955:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *      - Bits [30..24] is reserved
 956:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *      - Bits [23..16] indicates the logical sensor number of the sensor that 
 957:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *        detected a touch. If more than one sensor detected a touch for the CSD
 958:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *        widget, no status is reported as more than one touch is invalid for the
 959:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *        CSD matrix buttons widgets.
 960:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *      - Bits [15..8] indicates the active row number.
 961:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *      - Bits [7..0] indicates the active column number.
 962:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *    2. For the matrix buttons widgets with the CSX widgets, each bit (31..0)
 963:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *      corresponds to the TX/RX intersection.
 964:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *
 965:Generated_Source\PSoC4/CapSense_Structure.c **** *******************************************************************************/
